	(text "REGEN SHUNT (record section 5). Self-acting clamp, no firmware: U3 compares the divided\n  bus to U4's 1.24 V; R503 hysteresis.\nR501/R502/R503 348k/10k/3.01M: ON 44.5 V, OFF 43.2 V (1.4 V hysteresis, the OSSM alt\n  board's value). Legal above the GST360A36's 37.8 V worst OVP only because the input\n  section blocks reverse current.\nR509 || R510 || R511: Vishay D2TO35M 24R each = 8R (multi-pulse rated; element isolated\n  from the tab, tabs to GND over 0.8 mm via fields into the back sink). ~7 W continuous\n  total = 2.3 W each; 141 W peak = 47 W each.\nJ3 + JP501: external resistor. JP501 bridged = parallel with the on-board pair; cut =\n  external replaces it. Size Q501 for the lowest combined R.\nD503 SS310 freewheels the resistor-loop current back to +BUS at turn-off, so trace and\n  flying-lead inductance clamps at bus + 0.85 V. D501 stays as the backstop.\nU3 drives Q501's gate directly through R505 (TLV1805 push-pull, ~100 mA: ~0.7 us edges,\n  ~0.25 W worst case in Q501; slow edges keep L di/dt small, no driver or snubber needed).\n  R507/R508: gate pull-down + CLAMP_MON (2.98 V) to a P4 capture pin: on-time x V^2 / 8R =\n  clamp power, published over Valence. D502 lights while the clamp conducts. TH501 NTC\n  sits beside the D2TO35Ms -> SHUNT_TEMP (ADC1).\nU3 SHDN (active high) tied low: always armed. +12V from the 12 V buck, which starts from\n  the bus by itself. C501 filters buck noise off the divider.\nQ501 PSMN3R7-100BSE: its tab is the switch node (drain), NOT ground: give it its own\n  copper, not the grounded resistor via field."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
